1
00:00:00,030 --> 00:00:02,030
Cinderella

2
00:00:06,970 --> 00:00:11,870
Cinderella's Sister

3
00:00:40,790 --> 00:00:48,930
Cinderella's Sister

4
00:00:51,120 --> 00:00:52,800
Episode 15

5
00:01:13,280 --> 00:01:19,840
When that person sometimes goes to meet her old man from before then comes back home and smiles at me,

6
00:01:19,860 --> 00:01:26,780
emotions of anger, despair, and sadness take turns in overcoming me.

7
00:01:35,670 --> 00:01:39,060
I'd like to ask that person why she does that,

8
00:01:39,060 --> 00:01:43,900
but this foolish man is too scared to open his mouth that can't even say a word.

9
00:02:38,140 --> 00:02:40,420
Leave!

10
00:04:10,290 --> 00:04:13,430
The things you couldn't object to, Dad,

11
00:04:16,820 --> 00:04:20,170
I wanted to try.

12
00:04:21,510 --> 00:04:27,720
How she could do such a thing. Taking advantage of someone...

13
00:04:29,430 --> 00:04:34,410
And how she could do that to a person like you.

14
00:04:35,550 --> 00:04:38,130
How she could try to fool you.

15
00:04:40,550 --> 00:04:44,010
I could've told her to leave immediately.

16
00:04:46,580 --> 00:04:48,280
But... I didn't do that, Dad.

17
00:04:54,900 --> 00:05:01,220
I don't want to kick her out so simply.

18
00:05:06,660 --> 00:05:12,280
I didn't want to resolve it so simply,

19
00:05:12,280 --> 00:05:16,830
♫ ♫I am living day after day

20
00:05:16,830 --> 00:05:19,610
so I held back.

21
00:05:19,610 --> 00:05:28,590
♫ In your name when tears appear, ♫I

22
00:05:28,620 --> 00:05:30,350
♫  can't bear it ♫I

23
00:05:30,350 --> 00:05:32,630
What I'm going to do...

24
00:05:32,630 --> 00:05:37,620
So I can't laugh

25
00:05:37,620 --> 00:05:40,030
Wait and see, Dad.

26
00:06:38,680 --> 00:06:41,260
You were going to tell Unni?

27
00:06:42,510 --> 00:06:47,680
You're going tell Unni that I've found out?

28
00:06:49,030 --> 00:06:51,600
You don't need to.

29
00:06:53,340 --> 00:06:57,730
Mom.

30
00:07:00,020 --> 00:07:05,760
If Unni finds out, I'm sure it'll be noisy. I don't want it to be noisy at all.

31
00:07:05,760 --> 00:07:11,740
Let's just keep quiet and let this pass.

32
00:07:17,600 --> 00:07:21,180
Don't think of anything else.

33
00:07:21,220 --> 00:07:32,380
Mom you just quietly live as the madam of Woon Hak Pavilion and as my mom.

34
00:07:32,380 --> 00:07:35,550
You're going to live this way.

35
00:07:39,830 --> 00:07:43,970
Because of the problems with the contract, I'm sure Unni will constantly on the phone at the winery.

36
00:07:43,970 --> 00:07:48,460
Pack Unni a lunch box, Mom. I'll take it to her so that she can eat.

37
00:08:02,590 --> 00:08:04,850
I know you don't make the decisions,

38
00:08:04,850 --> 00:08:07,570
so please let me meet the person who does.

39
00:08:07,570 --> 00:08:09,860
Please do this for me.

40
00:08:09,860 --> 00:08:13,250
Sorry for coming out of the blue and asking for such a difficult favor

41
00:08:13,250 --> 00:08:17,240
after not having contacted you since we were classmates.

42
00:08:17,240 --> 00:08:20,140
But, I'll be sure to make it up to you.

43
00:08:20,140 --> 00:08:23,570
I won't ever forget your kindness. Please, do this for me.

44
00:08:23,580 --> 00:08:27,140
We do need the freeze dry producing equipment from your company.

45
00:08:27,150 --> 00:08:30,650
And of course we'll naturally cover all the expenses.

46
00:08:35,990 --> 00:08:39,380
I already sent these to you via email, but these are all the documents.

47
00:08:39,380 --> 00:08:41,710
If you get a chance, please read them.

48
00:08:43,750 --> 00:08:49,160
Hello? My name is Hong Gi Hoon, the one who called you before. I'm on my way there now-

49
00:09:00,600 --> 00:09:06,290
Anyway, you will meet me because I'm not going to give up.

50
00:09:06,290 --> 00:09:08,730
I'll see you in 10 minutes.

51
00:09:20,130 --> 00:09:22,290
So, he's from HongJoo Winery?

52
00:09:22,290 --> 00:09:26,810
Yes. He said he wanted to meet you.

53
00:09:27,950 --> 00:09:31,090
It seemed like he was really interested in your yeast.

54
00:09:33,760 --> 00:09:41,290
Right. Is there any relative named Jang Taek Geun in your family?

55
00:09:44,700 --> 00:09:48,540
Mom won't tell me.

56
00:09:52,380 --> 00:09:57,120
There is none. I already told you there wasn't.

57
00:10:01,810 --> 00:10:07,530
Is that so? I got it.

58
00:10:07,530 --> 00:10:09,810
What are you saying you got?

59
00:10:11,340 --> 00:10:16,580
Yes. You said there's no one.

60
00:10:18,510 --> 00:10:20,180
I'm just saying I got that.

61
00:10:25,000 --> 00:10:29,880
Let's go to Hong Joo Winery. To the person you met with before.

62
00:10:32,760 --> 00:10:37,340
I have to hear directly exactly what his intentions are.

63
00:10:39,200 --> 00:10:45,770
Go alone. I need to stay with Mom.

64
00:10:47,960 --> 00:10:52,150
It seems that Mom is longing for Dad lately.

65
00:10:54,720 --> 00:10:57,850
I need to stay with Mom.

66
00:11:03,940 --> 00:11:06,130
Why are you looking at me like that?

67
00:11:07,950 --> 00:11:11,490
Then, would you like to stay with Mom?

68
00:11:11,540 --> 00:11:15,030
I'll be the one going around for the cooperative work.

69
00:11:23,240 --> 00:11:29,400
This food... Please eat it before you go.

70
00:11:29,400 --> 00:11:32,390
Don't starve and stumble.

71
00:11:34,980 --> 00:11:38,630
How can you get skinnier day by day?

72
00:11:38,630 --> 00:11:41,650
That's why you keep collapsing so often.

73
00:12:03,020 --> 00:12:08,160
Is there any relative named Jang Taek Geun in your family?

74
00:12:54,330 --> 00:12:58,180
My Daughter

75
00:13:17,270 --> 00:13:20,310
We have to make sure that Ahjussi Jang doesn't show up again, Jeong Woo.

76
00:13:20,310 --> 00:13:22,790
Don't worry, he's not going to show up.

77
00:13:22,790 --> 00:13:26,310
He definitely can't show up again.

78
00:13:26,370 --> 00:13:28,460
I also asked him that.

79
00:13:28,460 --> 00:13:31,970
That if he's starving, to contact me without telling anything to you.

80
00:13:31,970 --> 00:13:35,620
He said he'd do that, so don't worry.

81
00:13:37,510 --> 00:13:41,670
Have you been eating? You didn't, right?

82
00:14:12,680 --> 00:14:17,000
It's delicious! Why did you make the kimbap, Mom?

83
00:14:18,200 --> 00:14:23,420
Joon Soo wants to eat gimbap, so I'm going to feed him some when he comes back from his kindergarten.

84
00:14:23,420 --> 00:14:27,150
Ah, I see.

85
00:14:29,760 --> 00:14:35,410
Leave that to Grandmother and Ahjumma. Let's go together to pick Joon Soo up, Mom.

86
00:14:42,810 --> 00:14:47,730
Let's wait in front of his kindergarten and bring him home.

87
00:14:47,730 --> 00:14:51,880
Why should we? The bus will bring him anyway.

88
00:14:53,700 --> 00:14:56,930
Grandmother from Yeon Cheon

89
00:14:56,930 --> 00:15:02,280
Yes, Grandmother.I wanted to call you but I completely forgot.

90
00:15:05,200 --> 00:15:08,650
Yes. Mom?

91
00:15:10,980 --> 00:15:13,090
What about Mom?

92
00:15:14,780 --> 00:15:20,700
I don't know what you're going to tell me, but please don't do it, Grandmother.

93
00:15:22,380 --> 00:15:27,930
I'll go and see you soon, so please don't tell me now.

94
00:15:27,930 --> 00:15:33,520
Yes. I'll hang up now. Yes, Grandmother, take care.

95
00:15:39,160 --> 00:15:42,360
Mom, hurry up.

96
00:16:06,340 --> 00:16:09,760
Why is he taking so long?

97
00:16:09,760 --> 00:16:14,070
Isn't it past the time he's supposed to come out? Right, Mom?

98
00:16:20,260 --> 00:16:24,690
Can't you tell me in advance how far you'll go?

99
00:16:24,690 --> 00:16:30,990
I don't know how far I'll go either. I'm sorry.

100
00:16:30,990 --> 00:16:35,820
Are you planning to go to the end?

101
00:16:35,820 --> 00:16:40,400
I am planning to go to the end.

102
00:16:40,400 --> 00:16:46,210
Alright then. It's not as though I don't have other ways either.

103
00:16:46,210 --> 00:16:52,530
What are you talking about? I'm not sure what you're talking about, but leave now.

104
00:16:52,530 --> 00:16:57,340
I'm expecting to receive a visitor and it's about time for her to arrive.

105
00:16:57,340 --> 00:17:00,090
Is it okay for you to run into them?

106
00:17:03,720 --> 00:17:07,330
What time did you say the meeting was with Dae Seong True Winemakers' Goo Eun Jo?

107
00:17:20,980 --> 00:17:23,910
I'll be nearby so call me when you're done, Noona.

108
00:17:23,910 --> 00:17:25,530
Okay.

109
00:18:36,400 --> 00:18:38,590
Don't worry.

110
00:18:38,590 --> 00:18:43,100
I don't want to tell anyone about you yet.

111
00:18:46,910 --> 00:18:50,160
I don't understand what you're talking about.

112
00:18:50,180 --> 00:18:55,540
An outstanding corporation such as Dae Seong True Winemakers is attempting to stand up utilizing Japanese corporate funds.

113
00:18:55,540 --> 00:18:58,300
I find that regretful so I spoke.

114
00:18:58,300 --> 00:19:04,340
Our company is probably much better than Japan, on a patriotic level.

115
00:19:04,340 --> 00:19:08,380
Is that why you interfered with our contract?

116
00:19:08,380 --> 00:19:13,330
Because it's more patriotic to accept Hong Joo Ga's investment rather than from a Japanese company?

117
00:19:13,330 --> 00:19:16,220
I'll get straight to the point.

118
00:19:16,220 --> 00:19:21,020
We'll support you so that you can only continue doing research on the yeast.

119
00:19:21,020 --> 00:19:24,580
I also won't touch Dae Seong True Winemaker's name.

120
00:19:25,910 --> 00:19:28,710
I sincerely think it's unfortunate

121
00:19:28,710 --> 00:19:33,280
that someone as incredible as Goo Dae Sung passed away.

122
00:19:33,280 --> 00:19:39,790
His name remaining in the company and products names...

123
00:19:39,790 --> 00:19:43,090
I believe that has meaning.

124
00:19:43,090 --> 00:19:48,660
So, in short it means that you want us to hand over Dae Seong True Winemakers.

125
00:19:48,660 --> 00:19:51,860
I'm not asking you to give it up for free.

126
00:19:54,500 --> 00:19:57,040
Thank you.

127
00:19:57,040 --> 00:19:59,280
You're thanking me?

128
00:19:59,280 --> 00:20:05,930
I hadn't known that Dae Seong True Winemakers had such a threatening potential.

129
00:20:05,930 --> 00:20:09,660
I'd been working hard because I have to build it up no matter what,

130
00:20:09,660 --> 00:20:14,680
but thank you for helping me realize that Dae Sung True Winemakers is large enough

131
00:20:14,680 --> 00:20:20,650
to make the country's largest rice winery, Hong Joo Ga, want to acquire it.

132
00:20:20,650 --> 00:20:25,410
It's also good to know that the conscience of such a large corporation only amounts to this much.

133
00:20:26,560 --> 00:20:31,200
Thank you. You've given me strength to get it back on its feet somehow.

134
00:20:33,590 --> 00:20:39,140
I'll just pretend I didn't hear your offer to provide support for my research on the yeast.

135
00:20:39,140 --> 00:20:45,880
You're saying this even though I told you the amount of money?

136
00:20:45,880 --> 00:20:49,820
I'm saying it's even more impossible because you told me the amount you'd pay.

137
00:20:49,820 --> 00:20:53,150
If you're willing to offer me that much money for the yeast that I've discovered,

138
00:20:53,150 --> 00:20:57,460
that means the market value of my yeast is worth multiples of that amount.

139
00:20:57,460 --> 00:21:01,740
Thank you for that too. That's become a large source of strength as well.

140
00:21:01,740 --> 00:21:06,050
If things go well, I'll repay you by buying you a meal.

141
00:21:07,840 --> 00:21:11,660
Also, I won't forget it.

142
00:21:12,960 --> 00:21:18,900
I won't forget a single thing you've done to us.

143
00:21:18,900 --> 00:21:23,300
I'll repay you for that too, so wait and be prepared.

144
00:21:52,640 --> 00:21:55,990
Mom, let's take a family photo.

145
00:21:57,250 --> 00:22:03,970
Mom, Eun Jo, Joon Soo and me...

146
00:22:06,030 --> 00:22:08,680
We don't have a family photo.

147
00:22:10,310 --> 00:22:13,710
We should've taken one when Dad was still here.

148
00:22:15,330 --> 00:22:18,130
But Dad was quite busy, I guess.

149
00:22:22,070 --> 00:22:24,630
Let's take one and hang it up.

150
00:22:25,540 --> 00:22:30,300
In your room, my room, and Unni's room.

151
00:22:31,440 --> 00:22:35,880
We should also print one for each family member to put in our wallets.

152
00:22:47,430 --> 00:22:49,450
Joon Soo!

153
00:22:50,910 --> 00:22:53,590
Joon Soo, no. Hurry and come down. Don't do that. It's dangerous.

154
00:22:53,590 --> 00:22:55,750
- No!
- Quick, come to Noona.

155
00:22:55,750 --> 00:23:00,840
A little girl like her actually dares to challenge

156
00:23:00,840 --> 00:23:07,420
the Song Kang Sook who has even beat God and the Buddha.

157
00:23:07,420 --> 00:23:11,520
A little puppy, who isn't even a day old, is showing her teeth

158
00:23:11,520 --> 00:23:16,480
at someone who has never even feared God or the Buddha.

159
00:23:18,780 --> 00:23:21,800
Let's play!

160
00:23:24,750 --> 00:23:30,090
That newborn puppy...is even scarier than a ghost.

161
00:23:53,220 --> 00:23:57,180
- Hyo Seon is here!
- Joon Soo is here!

162
00:23:59,980 --> 00:24:02,350
Mom!

163
00:24:07,680 --> 00:24:10,170
Mom isn't here.

164
00:24:12,180 --> 00:24:14,070
Not here?

165
00:24:34,450 --> 00:24:38,260
- Joon Soo.
- Yeah?

166
00:24:39,010 --> 00:24:43,290
Go ask Grandma for food and eat.

167
00:24:43,290 --> 00:24:45,040
Okay.

168
00:25:29,120 --> 00:25:34,470
You're leaving? How can you leave like this?

169
00:25:41,000 --> 00:25:44,310
You're leaving? How can you leave like this?

170
00:25:44,310 --> 00:25:47,640
How can you leave after the child grew feelings for you?

171
00:25:54,440 --> 00:25:58,720
This damn destiny, damn Song Kang Sook.

172
00:25:58,720 --> 00:26:04,400
Now I realize the worst part of my fate is this family.

173
00:26:04,400 --> 00:26:09,520
God, Buddha, thank you for at least making me realize now.

174
00:26:09,520 --> 00:26:13,720
You've finally come to your senses.

175
00:26:30,950 --> 00:26:33,120
Stay right there!

176
00:26:40,040 --> 00:26:43,500
Why am I seeing that scary woman?

177
00:26:43,500 --> 00:26:46,370
Why am I seeing that evil b*tch?

178
00:27:20,140 --> 00:27:25,720
Where are you going? You can't go! Who said you can go?

179
00:27:34,250 --> 00:27:36,340
Don't stop, Ajusshi.

180
00:28:33,430 --> 00:28:36,620
- Let me go!
- Where are you going?!

181
00:28:36,620 --> 00:28:40,200
Let go!

182
00:28:42,270 --> 00:28:44,850
Let go of me!

183
00:28:46,420 --> 00:28:48,340
Give me my bag!

184
00:28:59,530 --> 00:29:02,510
Let go! Let go, you b*tch. You evil b*tch.

185
00:29:02,510 --> 00:29:04,990
You demon! You're the worst in this world!

186
00:29:04,990 --> 00:29:08,430
You demon! Get your hands off me!

187
00:29:08,500 --> 00:29:11,600
Where are you going? You can't go.

188
00:29:11,600 --> 00:29:15,720
You have to live under my torture until the day you die, Mom.

189
00:29:15,720 --> 00:29:19,030
If I wanted to watch you run away, I would've kicked you out already.

190
00:29:19,030 --> 00:29:21,520
You think I wouldn't do anything?

191
00:29:21,520 --> 00:29:26,190
Why don't you just swear at me instead?! Call me a b*tch, call me a wh*re.

192
00:29:26,190 --> 00:29:29,990
Why do you have to call me Mom with that faint smile on your face?

193
00:29:29,990 --> 00:29:33,490
You're a hundred times scarier than I am, you know that?

194
00:29:33,490 --> 00:29:37,890
Watch your mouth, Mom. Someone might hear you.

195
00:29:37,890 --> 00:29:40,770
A wh*re?

196
00:29:40,770 --> 00:29:42,830
What?

197
00:29:42,830 --> 00:29:45,530
That is something out of this world,

198
00:29:45,530 --> 00:29:50,990
just for you, God and me to know.

199
00:29:50,990 --> 00:29:56,640
Even God doesn't want anyone else to know, so keep your mouth shut!

200
00:29:56,640 --> 00:29:59,320
How can you say such words?

201
00:29:59,320 --> 00:30:02,550
Where did you learn to be so rude?

202
00:30:02,550 --> 00:30:04,920
How can you do this to your father?

203
00:30:04,920 --> 00:30:08,590
How can you do that with a human masK? It's better to curse at me, you bitch.

204
00:30:08,590 --> 00:30:12,290
If there were not Joon Soo between you and me,

205
00:30:12,290 --> 00:30:14,750
I would also have done that.

206
00:30:16,670 --> 00:30:21,250
My little brother, Joon Soo...

207
00:30:23,580 --> 00:30:27,520
My father's son, Joon Soo...

208
00:30:28,610 --> 00:30:32,600
How could I insult my father's son?

209
00:30:36,310 --> 00:30:42,290
Should I try it? Should I spit in Joon Soo's face

210
00:30:42,290 --> 00:30:46,660
and call his mother a wh*re?

211
00:30:46,660 --> 00:30:48,500
Say it! Why can't you?!

212
00:30:48,500 --> 00:30:51,910
How can I spit in my father son's face?!

213
00:30:59,590 --> 00:31:01,080
Oh no...

214
00:31:01,080 --> 00:31:03,030
Don't touch!

215
00:31:05,260 --> 00:31:10,550
Don't try to apologize. I won't believe you.

216
00:31:11,890 --> 00:31:15,530
Are you trying to ask me for forgiveness, Mom?

217
00:31:15,530 --> 00:31:21,480
The person who should forgive you is already dead! Why are you begging me?

218
00:31:23,350 --> 00:31:27,660
Just live like this forever.

219
00:31:27,660 --> 00:31:30,780
Live as a sinner.

220
00:31:30,780 --> 00:31:33,670
Do you think I'll forgive you?

221
00:31:33,670 --> 00:31:37,380
Do you think I'll let you live with ease?

222
00:32:57,350 --> 00:32:59,100
Get on my back.

223
00:33:02,770 --> 00:33:06,340
Get on my back, you awful brat.

224
00:33:35,490 --> 00:33:38,040
Call ended

225
00:33:43,750 --> 00:33:47,780
Your call cannot be connected. After the beep, you will be connected to voic--.

226
00:33:51,730 --> 00:33:54,350
Where in the world are you and what are you doing?

227
00:33:54,350 --> 00:33:58,420
With a whole mountain of work, you neglected it and are putting on antics like this.

228
00:33:58,420 --> 00:34:01,650
I want to let you know. I truly will not leave you alone.

229
00:34:13,550 --> 00:34:16,940
Jeong Woo. Jeong Woo!

230
00:34:23,130 --> 00:34:24,770
For now, we're going to make the wine.

231
00:34:24,790 --> 00:34:29,750
We're going to make the wine and give some to the village associations, funerals, and feasts.

232
00:34:29,750 --> 00:34:33,530
I'm going to do that so people don't forget our wine.

233
00:34:33,530 --> 00:34:36,420
Get ready.

234
00:34:36,420 --> 00:34:37,730
But, where are you going now?

235
00:34:37,730 --> 00:34:40,680
To the research lab. Let go of me.

236
00:34:40,680 --> 00:34:43,820
It's late, go tomorrow. Do you know what time it is?

237
00:34:43,820 --> 00:34:46,770
Stop fooling around and finish up what you were doing so you can get off work.

238
00:34:57,040 --> 00:34:59,260
Go in, I have something to say to you.

239
00:34:59,260 --> 00:35:01,910
- What kind of person are you?
- I said let's go in.

240
00:35:01,910 --> 00:35:05,190
You plan on behaving as such and have thoughts of receiving wages from someone else's company?

241
00:35:05,190 --> 00:35:08,910
What kind of person are you? What are you thinking?!

242
00:35:08,910 --> 00:35:12,780
I don't need a worker like you. Resign immediately.

243
00:35:12,780 --> 00:35:17,260
We... can make wine, Eun Jo.

244
00:35:20,890 --> 00:35:23,680
The freeze dried line that the Japanese had cancelled

245
00:35:23,680 --> 00:35:27,100
was identical to probiotics made by pharmaceutical companies.

246
00:35:27,100 --> 00:35:31,770
I went to around ten of those places, and one place returned the call.

247
00:35:34,230 --> 00:35:35,670
You got a call?

248
00:35:35,680 --> 00:35:39,300
Their conditions are demanding though.

249
00:35:39,300 --> 00:35:42,890
First, the expenses will be high for a while.

250
00:35:42,890 --> 00:35:46,610
I will carefully consider the costs and benefits from this point forward.

251
00:35:46,610 --> 00:35:49,860
If the value is worth enough for us to bear the expense.

252
00:35:49,860 --> 00:35:53,920
I'll search for a way that doesn't harm Dae Seong True Winemakers.

253
00:35:53,920 --> 00:35:59,950
If the expenses are still too much, I'm going to meet them again and try to negotiate the price further.

254
00:36:02,210 --> 00:36:03,490
What's second?

255
00:36:03,540 --> 00:36:09,950
The second is that they found out the possibility of using the yeast you discovered as a medical raw material.

256
00:36:10,810 --> 00:36:14,830
It won't be right away but after some time

257
00:36:14,830 --> 00:36:17,990
you'll have to cooperate with them on the research.

258
00:36:17,990 --> 00:36:20,920
Of course, this is top secret.

259
00:36:22,660 --> 00:36:25,980
Is there a third condition?

260
00:36:25,980 --> 00:36:31,280
After the summer break, I have to work for their company.

261
00:36:36,990 --> 00:36:38,720
What?

262
00:36:41,230 --> 00:36:44,190
The person in-charge of the pharmaceutical company I met with

263
00:36:44,190 --> 00:36:48,530
is my seonbae, who attended the same school, when I studied in America.

264
00:36:51,900 --> 00:36:54,530
She said she needs me.

265
00:36:56,130 --> 00:37:00,380
I said I would do it.

266
00:37:02,400 --> 00:37:07,470
If I'm going to go, we need to stand Dae Seong True Winemakers on its feet now.

267
00:37:10,460 --> 00:37:13,350
We need to raise it up firmly so that it wouldn't tremble

268
00:37:13,350 --> 00:37:15,810
even if someone tries touching it or shaking it up.

269
00:37:18,840 --> 00:37:20,350
You ...

270
00:37:22,270 --> 00:37:24,210
said you'd do it?

271
00:37:27,140 --> 00:37:28,910
Yeah.

272
00:37:35,140 --> 00:37:37,440
So, you're leaving here?

273
00:37:41,400 --> 00:37:43,130
Yeah.

274
00:37:45,940 --> 00:37:48,450
So,

275
00:37:51,530 --> 00:37:54,470
you've promised to leave Dae Seong True Winemakers.

276
00:37:58,860 --> 00:38:03,070
Yeah. That's right.

277
00:38:11,470 --> 00:38:15,780
I promise I'll devote my life to work until I leave.

278
00:38:15,780 --> 00:38:17,750
Believe me.

279
00:39:15,410 --> 00:39:19,660
It's been more than an hour. How long are you going to be like this?

280
00:39:23,560 --> 00:39:26,390
Starting from a long time ago,

281
00:39:28,290 --> 00:39:33,840
I didn't look forward to anything when I opened my eyes every morning.

282
00:39:36,090 --> 00:39:39,380
I would either wake up in some man's house

283
00:39:40,340 --> 00:39:45,980
or some hotel room. It was always either one of the two.

284
00:39:47,700 --> 00:39:53,960
The words I heard most often were tirades from Mom in the morning.

285
00:39:56,300 --> 00:40:02,130
To the tirading mom, the curses those men pour out onto her.

286
00:40:03,220 --> 00:40:05,990
The sounds of the shattering of household goods.

287
00:40:09,530 --> 00:40:11,910
It was like that.

288
00:40:13,640 --> 00:40:16,790
Starting from one day,

289
00:40:16,790 --> 00:40:19,570
I didn't hear those sounds anymore.

290
00:40:20,950 --> 00:40:23,980
I thought that it would just be temporary,

291
00:40:23,980 --> 00:40:27,020
and that I'd hear what I didn't want to hear again.

292
00:40:28,150 --> 00:40:32,330
I didn't believe it, since it was a peace that would be broken soon.

293
00:40:34,280 --> 00:40:39,720
Because if I believed it and was betrayed, I'd be the one in pain.

294
00:40:43,260 --> 00:40:47,350
But still, no matter how many days passed,

295
00:40:47,350 --> 00:40:53,780
I couldn't hear my mom cursing. It seemed too good to be true.

296
00:40:56,690 --> 00:40:59,210
And then...

297
00:41:00,170 --> 00:41:04,610
Opening my eyes in the morning was becoming fun.

298
00:41:08,320 --> 00:41:11,320
I wanted to sleep early at night.

299
00:41:12,950 --> 00:41:16,870
Because once I slept and woke up, it'd be morning.

300
00:41:19,020 --> 00:41:24,070
Since I need to sleep and wake up in the morning

301
00:41:25,980 --> 00:41:30,420
for another day with him to begin.

302
00:41:34,490 --> 00:41:40,980
Every time I turned my face, there was someone who made me happy just be being there.

303
00:41:43,150 --> 00:41:48,380
How dare I... I didn't even expect much.

304
00:41:50,530 --> 00:41:54,150
No matter where I went,

305
00:41:54,150 --> 00:41:58,590
if that person were there, that was enough for me.

306
00:42:02,810 --> 00:42:06,120
Because even if I didn't see him for a little while,

307
00:42:06,140 --> 00:42:13,460
When I saw him again, I felt the joy I may have felt from not having seen someone in 100 million years.

308
00:42:14,480 --> 00:42:16,680
Award

309
00:42:16,680 --> 00:42:19,500
That was enough for me.

310
00:42:21,050 --> 00:42:26,710
Whenever you hold that in your hand, think of me.

311
00:42:28,970 --> 00:42:34,780
Was that too much to ask for?

312
00:42:36,980 --> 00:42:43,440
When just seeing him was enough for me...

313
00:42:45,840 --> 00:42:48,200
He left.

314
00:42:49,460 --> 00:42:54,320
♫  In your name when tears appear,  ♫

315
00:42:54,320 --> 00:42:56,200
But...

316
00:42:58,820 --> 00:43:00,860
He said he's leaving again.

317
00:43:02,470 --> 00:43:06,960
♫  So I can't laugh  ♫

318
00:43:06,990 --> 00:43:10,880
He said he'd leave again.

319
00:43:18,170 --> 00:43:23,260
Living feels like hell.

320
00:43:26,700 --> 00:43:30,030
Should I stop him from going?

321
00:43:32,330 --> 00:43:35,570
Should I snap his legs?

322
00:43:39,880 --> 00:43:42,320
Can you do that for me?

323
00:43:48,610 --> 00:43:53,470
If you can, can you try?

324
00:44:04,110 --> 00:44:06,110
Don't cry.

325
00:44:13,330 --> 00:44:15,300
Don't cry.

326
00:44:22,080 --> 00:44:24,460
It's for the best.

327
00:44:26,410 --> 00:44:28,680
If he leaves this time,

328
00:44:30,490 --> 00:44:33,070
he probably won't come back.

329
00:44:35,710 --> 00:44:37,360
If he doesn't come back,

330
00:44:40,170 --> 00:44:42,780
he won't leave again either.

331
00:44:47,500 --> 00:44:49,590
It's for the best.

332
00:44:53,970 --> 00:44:58,340
It really is, Jeong Woo.

333
00:45:06,520 --> 00:45:08,500
Dae Seong True Winemakers Takju Development Budgeting

334
00:45:10,640 --> 00:45:15,170
Can't you tell me in advance how far you'll go?

335
00:45:15,170 --> 00:45:22,470
I don't know how far I'll go either. I'm sorry.

336
00:45:22,470 --> 00:45:26,660
Are you going to go all the way?

337
00:45:26,660 --> 00:45:30,850
I'm going all the way.

338
00:45:40,070 --> 00:45:44,200
No! I said no!

339
00:45:44,200 --> 00:45:46,660
Stay still!

340
00:45:48,240 --> 00:45:52,560
Where are you touching? Don't touch me.

341
00:45:52,560 --> 00:45:55,830
You said you don't want to go to the hospital. You should at least put some ointment on.

342
00:45:55,830 --> 00:45:57,940
Will you be able to walk like this?

343
00:45:57,940 --> 00:46:02,210
Even if I can't walk, it's my problem! It's none of your business.

344
00:46:13,070 --> 00:46:15,000
What is this?

345
00:46:18,160 --> 00:46:20,180
I asked what is this?

346
00:46:26,760 --> 00:46:30,510
I hurt my soles, so I need to apply some ointment.

347
00:46:30,510 --> 00:46:34,190
Mom keeps hurting me.

348
00:46:34,190 --> 00:46:36,310
How did you get hurt?

349
00:46:43,820 --> 00:46:49,490
Apply it gently, Mom. It hurts.

350
00:46:54,650 --> 00:46:56,610
Lift your foot up.

351
00:47:36,560 --> 00:47:38,910
Have a good meal.

352
00:47:49,730 --> 00:47:54,020
It's beef leg bone broth. I've been craving it.

353
00:47:54,020 --> 00:47:56,600
Pick up your spoon, Mom.

354
00:48:31,570 --> 00:48:34,650
What are you doing?

355
00:48:34,650 --> 00:48:36,790
I'm putting salt in.

356
00:48:44,240 --> 00:48:46,040
What?

357
00:48:53,690 --> 00:48:57,500
You can't taste anything, so you keep putting salt in?

358
00:49:00,420 --> 00:49:02,790
It's not salty at all.

359
00:49:02,790 --> 00:49:05,290
Did you catch a cold or something?

360
00:49:05,290 --> 00:49:08,490
If you're really sick, you can't taste anything.

361
00:49:08,490 --> 00:49:10,500
No.

362
00:49:13,720 --> 00:49:15,340
Are you really okay?

363
00:49:15,340 --> 00:49:17,600
I'm fine.

364
00:49:21,440 --> 00:49:23,260
You...

365
00:49:36,220 --> 00:49:38,850
I said I'm fine! Why are you being like this?

366
00:49:38,850 --> 00:49:41,810
Stop talking and lie down.

367
00:49:41,810 --> 00:49:44,700
I said I'm fine!

368
00:49:44,700 --> 00:49:46,680
Mom!

369
00:49:47,970 --> 00:49:52,860
Your temperature is over 40 degrees! It's strange that you don't feel anything.

370
00:49:52,860 --> 00:49:57,760
Let's try to get your fever down first. I'll go get the oriental medicine Grandfather from the clinic.

371
00:50:04,030 --> 00:50:08,640
Mom, there's something really wrong with her. Get the grandfather to take a look at her,

372
00:50:08,640 --> 00:50:11,780
and if he says there's something wrong, we'll go to the hospital.

373
00:50:13,050 --> 00:50:16,070
Okay. Hurry and go to work.

374
00:50:18,760 --> 00:50:22,890
I'm taking care of things at work. Don't worry.

375
00:50:24,520 --> 00:50:28,130
- Really?
- Yes.

376
00:50:28,130 --> 00:50:33,520
Things are going well. I think the pharmaceutical company can lend us their freeze-dry production line.

377
00:50:34,840 --> 00:50:38,450
- Really?
- Yes.

378
00:50:40,760 --> 00:50:44,830
Hurry and go. Don't trouble her with work.

379
00:50:46,120 --> 00:50:47,960
Rest up.

380
00:50:58,760 --> 00:51:01,700
You still have the energy to fight with me when you have such a high fever?

381
00:51:01,700 --> 00:51:04,710
Yes. I'm full of energy.

382
00:51:04,710 --> 00:51:07,500
Close your eyes and sleep.

383
00:51:07,500 --> 00:51:09,650
No!

384
00:51:15,040 --> 00:51:17,050
Go away.

385
00:51:20,020 --> 00:51:23,000
I've never seen someone like you.

386
00:51:23,000 --> 00:51:27,710
I've committed so many sins, so maybe meeting someone like you

387
00:51:28,950 --> 00:51:33,580
is fate... fate that brought us together.

388
00:51:35,970 --> 00:51:40,690
Everything before wasn't punishment. This is my real punishment.

389
00:51:43,840 --> 00:51:48,680
This isn't even the beginning yet.

390
00:52:10,920 --> 00:52:12,670
There is a special person.

391
00:52:12,670 --> 00:52:15,050
A special person?

392
00:52:15,050 --> 00:52:17,610
Then, how special am I to you?

393
00:52:26,280 --> 00:52:31,190
It's so nice here! This is where rice wine is stored.

394
00:52:33,390 --> 00:52:35,330
I might get drunk here.

395
00:52:38,950 --> 00:52:41,930
- This tastes so good.
- It does, right?

396
00:52:41,930 --> 00:52:45,320
If I get drunk because of this, you have to take care of me, okay?

397
00:52:54,690 --> 00:52:58,600
- What's going on in there?
- I don't know either.

398
00:53:28,750 --> 00:53:31,270
Dae Seong True Winemaker

399
00:53:31,270 --> 00:53:37,220
I've listed out the expenses. I've also marked what needs to be reduced.

400
00:53:37,220 --> 00:53:41,690
In my opinion, the best choice is to use this production line.

401
00:53:41,690 --> 00:53:44,700
It's best to hurry and make a decision.

402
00:53:44,700 --> 00:53:47,850
My sunbae from the pharmaceutical company just left.

403
00:53:47,850 --> 00:53:52,640
She said she wanted to come take a look, so I told her to come. Things look positive.

404
00:53:53,970 --> 00:53:57,610
Is it the sunbae that scouted you?

405
00:53:58,880 --> 00:54:01,770
Yeah, that sunbae.

406
00:54:04,920 --> 00:54:07,250
She laughs a lot.

407
00:54:08,810 --> 00:54:14,400
Yeah, she's someone who always makes people laugh.

408
00:54:14,400 --> 00:54:16,730
She's a happy person.

409
00:54:19,930 --> 00:54:22,350
You were laughing a lot with her too.

410
00:54:23,620 --> 00:54:25,070
Yeah,

411
00:54:26,200 --> 00:54:29,720
she makes all the people around her laugh.

412
00:54:42,430 --> 00:54:47,180
Let me know what else we need until we make a decision.

413
00:54:47,180 --> 00:54:51,410
- Okay.
- Are you going to the research lab?

414
00:54:51,410 --> 00:54:53,180
Yeah.

415
00:54:53,180 --> 00:54:55,340
Should I take you there?

416
00:55:00,150 --> 00:55:02,260
You must be relieved.

417
00:55:02,260 --> 00:55:06,270
- What?
- About getting a better job.

418
00:55:06,270 --> 00:55:13,290
After all, you're someone who should've been working in marketing at a huge company from the start.

419
00:55:13,290 --> 00:55:19,640
You just didn't have any excuse to leave me and Hyo Seon after Hyo Seon's father passed.

420
00:55:19,640 --> 00:55:25,380
Right? You must think you've finally found a blessing in this mess.

421
00:55:29,130 --> 00:55:33,790
Congratulations. It's great for you.

422
00:55:38,840 --> 00:55:42,500
Yeah. Thank you.

423
00:55:46,220 --> 00:55:50,930
Who was the girl messing around with you by the lake yesterday?

424
00:56:19,600 --> 00:56:23,360
- Good work, everyone.
- Good work.

425
00:56:27,830 --> 00:56:29,830
Hi, Sunbae.

426
00:56:30,850 --> 00:56:32,580
Yes.

427
00:56:33,960 --> 00:56:40,850
Really? Yeah. Are you sure?

428
00:56:42,250 --> 00:56:46,910
Yes. I got it. Thank you, Sunbae.

429
00:57:35,320 --> 00:57:39,840
You can't run away. You can't run away!

430
00:57:41,140 --> 00:57:46,590
You can't run away. You can't run away.

431
00:58:06,220 --> 00:58:12,200
You're really punishing me cruelly.

432
00:58:17,320 --> 00:58:25,530
You two are really crueler than I am.

433
00:58:28,170 --> 00:58:32,530
Dae Seong True Cooperative's production line has started.

434
00:58:32,530 --> 00:58:35,950
The freeze dried yeast from Nihon pharmaceutical

435
00:58:35,950 --> 00:58:40,300
has arrived at Dae Seong True Winemaker's factory.

436
00:58:40,300 --> 00:58:43,700
They've started production?

437
00:58:43,700 --> 00:58:46,510
Yes.

438
00:58:46,510 --> 00:58:49,510
They have a buyer?

439
00:58:49,510 --> 00:58:51,680
Yes.

440
00:58:53,550 --> 00:58:57,020
- You said there is?
- Yes.

441
00:58:57,020 --> 00:58:59,110
Who is it?

442
00:58:59,110 --> 00:59:04,530
Gi Hoon successfully persuaded Miura-san.

443
00:59:04,530 --> 00:59:08,530
They already received a dumping price for Hong Joo Ga's wine,

444
00:59:08,530 --> 00:59:12,200
so it wouldn't hurt them much if it doesn't sell.

445
00:59:12,200 --> 00:59:17,640
What did you say? Are you serious now?

446
00:59:18,610 --> 00:59:24,220
- The taste...
- The taste?
- They found that the taste of Dae Seong True Winemakers' takju

447
00:59:24,220 --> 00:59:29,960
is much better than Hongjoo Family's in market research in Japan.

448
00:59:29,960 --> 00:59:34,460
Other alcohol distribution companies seem to be showing interest in them as well.

449
00:59:34,460 --> 00:59:39,720
It's also because our wine has been going around for almost free due to us dumping,

450
00:59:39,720 --> 00:59:44,330
so they had a lot of chances to compare our wine with Dae Seong True Winemakers is another reason.

451
00:59:44,330 --> 00:59:51,400
It seems product dumping was a big mistake.

452
00:59:54,060 --> 00:59:57,400
Do you have anything else to say?

453
00:59:57,400 --> 01:00:01,390
You're reporting this so shamelessly?

454
01:00:01,390 --> 01:00:04,890
Do you have anything else to report, Head Manager Park?

455
01:00:05,860 --> 01:00:08,690
Yes, I do.

456
01:00:12,290 --> 01:00:13,320
Resignation Letter

457
01:00:14,480 --> 01:00:19,530
I believe you'll accept this. I'll see myself off.

458
01:00:35,040 --> 01:00:38,770
Only that one? Go quickly and come back to take more boxes.

459
01:00:38,770 --> 01:00:43,030
Put it on straight like that, stretched and flat like so

460
01:00:57,490 --> 01:01:02,070
Hello, Dong Soo? Wait a moment.

461
01:01:03,800 --> 01:01:05,950
Yes. What are you saying?

462
01:01:05,950 --> 01:01:10,530
I found out a few things, but I had to confirm some things first.

463
01:01:10,530 --> 01:01:15,070
About the export scam in Japan, apparently it was Hong Joo Ga...

464
01:01:15,070 --> 01:01:16,840
Hong Joo Ga?

465
01:01:16,840 --> 01:01:22,340
Hong Joo Ga had something to do with it. There's also something else that's strange.

466
01:01:33,240 --> 01:01:38,160
The Hyeong, Hong Gi Joon, in your company is that family's youngest son.

467
01:01:38,160 --> 01:01:40,510
Did you know that?

468
01:01:53,940 --> 01:01:55,780
Eun Jo.

469
01:02:03,560 --> 01:02:07,170
Business K: The person who lives again through Dae Seong Saccaromycetes.

470
01:02:09,560 --> 01:02:14,050
Everything is done. It's all over now.

471
01:02:27,860 --> 01:02:31,770
♫  It must be you  ♫

472
01:02:31,820 --> 01:02:35,240
♫  I cannot be without you  ♫

473
01:02:35,270 --> 01:02:42,190
♫  Like this for another day, month or year  ♫

474
01:02:42,190 --> 01:02:45,770
♫ I don't mind even if I am hurt. ♫

475
01:02:45,770 --> 01:02:48,940
- Let's talk.
- No! I don't want to listen.

476
01:02:48,940 --> 01:02:50,830
Eun Jo!

477
01:02:51,710 --> 01:02:53,630
Where are you? Did you go to Dong Soo?

478
01:02:53,630 --> 01:02:56,880
Dong Soo, you can't say anything to Hyo Seon.

479
01:02:56,880 --> 01:02:58,710
I heard.

480
01:03:01,390 --> 01:03:05,790
She left in such a state, and you just let her go alone?

481
01:03:05,790 --> 01:03:10,470
Is there something wrong with Hyo Seon's taste buds? You should take her to the hospital.

482
01:03:11,950 --> 01:03:18,000
♫ Can't you hear my voice? ♫

483
01:03:18,000 --> 01:03:25,130
♫ Come to me.
Even if I live again ♫

484
01:03:25,130 --> 01:03:29,310
♫ No matter how many times I am reborn ♫

485
01:03:29,310 --> 01:03:36,010
♫ There isn't a day that I can live without you. ♫

486
01:03:36,010 --> 01:03:39,120
♫ The love I will protect ♫

487
01:03:39,120 --> 01:03:43,570
♫ The love I love because for me ♫

488
01:03:43,570 --> 01:03:48,730
♫ Yes, if it's just you, it is enough ♫
